==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~12 seconds<sup>300f~360f</sup>.
*3 [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Kory|Kories]] spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Kory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You will need to complete this level quickly if you do not wish to get overwhelmed by Coffin Zoges and Kories stacking up.

The easiest way to beat this stage is to bring [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]] and some attack up combos like [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]], alongside worker up and/or starting money up combos. A. Bahamut will knock Kory back with every hit, thus killing him, then can go for the base while Coffin Zoge gets killed multiple times in the process. This can work even if Kory doesn't get knocked back every attack, as, after the first hit, he can still kill Kory easily if every other attack deals a knockback, meaning that A. Bahamut just needs 1/6 of Kory's health as attack power to work.

For 2-crown and up, the combination of [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]] and [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Heroic Musashi]] can also make this stage a joke. If you have Bahamut's Explosion talent, you can simply save up money, not put out anything, and then send Bahamut and you win.

A Lv.40 Awakened Bahamut knocks back the Kory in a single hit in 1 and 4-crown difficulties. The sub-chapter that this stage is in has the highest Beast Bone drop rate out of all others. Starting Money Up Combos and nothing but a single Awakened Bahamut can lead to an incredibly fast farming method for said resource.

